====================================================================================
(1) THE FIGURATE LADDER  sum_{n>=k} 1/C(n,k) = k/(k-1)  — VERIFIED + telescoping proof
====================================================================================
  k=2: partial through n=3999 = 1.99949987496874   exact finite remainder = 7996/3999  match=True
  k=3: partial through n=3999 = 1.49999981235929   exact finite remainder = 3997000/2664667  match=True
  k=4: partial through n=3999 = 1.33333333320815   exact finite remainder = 14200898664/10650673999  match=True
  k=5: partial through n=3999 = 1.24999999999988   exact finite remainder = 13300029156250/10640023325001  match=True
  k=6: partial through n=3999 = 1.2   exact finite remainder = 17002757273351596/14168964394459665  match=True
  k=7: partial through n=3999 = 1.16666666666667   exact finite remainder = 2829542189573595100/2425321876777367229  match=True
  k=8: partial through n=3999 = 1.14285714285714   exact finite remainder = 25824827343925406254384/22596723925934730472593  match=True
  telescoping: 1/C(n,k) = k/(k-1) [1/C(n-1,k-1) - 1/C(n,k-1)]  (identity, proven in THM)
  k=1 (harmonic, vertices): k/(k-1) -> infinity  = the DIVERGENT origin of the ladder.
  k->inf: k/(k-1) -> 1.  Ladder of sums: inf, 2, 3/2, 4/3, 5/4, ... -> 1.

